   "Northwind-negotiator": "competing",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "compromising",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "competing"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S1 is strict: all thermal incidents reported within 24h, complete report within 10 days, and customer notice within 72h. S2 sets a 55°C test and 5% permanent limit with exact rates to customers and regulators, but lacks a bounded sales-stop or remediation consequence, leaving open-ended corrective action. S3 requires new-unit shut-off and a 6-year retrofit with feasibility escape; S4 allows equivalent containment from 36 months; S5 mandates recall at 8/100k with prompt notices and no automatic permanent ban."
 },
